oMLX
----
Parts of TyloInfer's Metal scheduling and model-specific kernels are adapted from
oMLX, with TyloInfer-specific model layouts and runtime integration.

Copyright (c) 2026 Apple Inc.
License: Apache License 2.0 (`LICENSE`)
Source: https://github.com/jundot/omlx

The balanced memory-budget and release-credit accounting follow
omlx/process_memory_enforcer.py, adapted to TyloInfer's managed runtime processes.

The Flash-Next grouped decode-submission policy is adapted from oMLX's
Qwen4 eager dispatch in language.py at revision
87460f4d50de79aef9b67e99e215c31f0a89b445, with TyloInfer-specific single-token and
component-profiling guards.
The singleton selected-block GQA gather/SDPA path follows
contiguous_causal_gathered_qsa_decode in qsa_fast.py at the same revision;
TyloInfer fuses K/V gathering and retains a validity mask for invalid block IDs.
The single-token Gated DeltaNet step layout follows
qwen4_decode_step_fused in qwen35_gdn_prework.py at revision
107e271ad449e2a9a060ec9a76d0c1d42724a2e2; TyloInfer retains its FP32 recurrent
state, transposed cache contract, and existing reduction order.
The Qwen4 QSA prefill pipeline, fused indexer-score and chronological FP32
top-k kernels follow qsa_fast.py, language.py and the native DSA indexer at
revision a435a3736071286fdb2b74f486b3505f23f3c194. The sparse main kernels
adapt its NAX half2 and tiled GQA paths; TyloInfer retains its quantized projections
and cache interfaces. TyloInfer's prefill-only NAX variant packs a single FP16
probability term and uses a two-barrier score exchange, retaining FP32 scores,
softmax and accumulation.
The shared non-Dspark MTP depth controller, performance handoff, retry policy
and cross-request timing estimates are adapted from batch_generator.py at
revision a435a3736071286fdb2b74f486b3505f23f3c194, translated to C++ for
TyloInfer's Metal and CUDA generation engines.
Copyright 2025 oMLX contributors
License: Apache License 2.0 (`LICENSE`)

TyloInfer's continuous-batch MTP depth policy is adapted from oMLX's BatchPolicy
and ParkMemory algorithms, with native coroutine and per-request cache
integration.
Reference: omlx/patches/mlx_lm_mtp/batch_policy.py

The upstream Qwen4 decode-step kernel carries an adaptation from mlx-serve.
Copyright (c) 2026 David Dalcu
License: MIT (`LICENSES/mlx-serve-MIT.txt`)
Source: https://github.com/ddalcu/mlx-serve

MLX
---
The grouped QSA decode kernel follows the online softmax reduction order of
the MLX v0.32.4 vector SDPA kernel, with separate FP16 K/V inputs per request.
DFlash2 draft attention follows the same reduction order and reads BF16 K/V
directly from each request's cache.
Copyright (c) 2024 Apple Inc.
License: MIT (`LICENSES/MLX-MIT.txt`)
Source: https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx

